      "value": "@{6223dd335cb08367f48eba41|full_name}: Input is no longer frame rate dependent.\nWith this update of Beta, the frame rate of the application and the mouse and controller stick swivel inputs are now completely separated.\n(The mouse was originally separated, but the app itself still seems to be designed to assume the frame rate.)\nPresumably, the app's turning process itself is still likely to be frame-rate dependent.\n(The mouse is in trouble, it shouldn't be doing it, but it is using old code to make the turning speed dependent on the frame rate. As a result, even with this BETA, when encountering a scene with high processing load, the turning speed increases in the opposite direction.)\nThe easiest solution would be to replacement the mouse and controller stick turning process on the BETA....\nTranslated with www.DeepL.com/Translator (free version)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
